  <ferc:DisclosureOfSignificantEventThatRespondentParticipatesInACashManagementProgramsTextBlock id="f-13" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-left:36pt;padding-right:18pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:4.11pt"&gt;13.N/A&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfSignificantEventThatRespondentParticipatesInACashManagementProgramsTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantDisclosuresRegardingTheFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-14" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-left:36pt;padding-right:18pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:120%;padding-left:11.34pt"&gt;Overview Of UGI Sunbury, LLC&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;a.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:11.34pt"&gt;Corporate Structure &amp;amp; Control&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:72pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;The Respondent is a limited liability company formed on December 16, 2014 under the laws of the State of Delaware, whose principal place of business is Wyomissing, Pennsylvania. As an LLC, the Respondent did not issue shares of stock or other similar securities. Rather, its equity is in the form of Membership Interests. 100% of the Membership Interests of the Respondent are owned by UGI Energy Services, LLC (&#8220;UGIES&#8221;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;b.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:11.34pt"&gt;Business &amp;amp; Facilities Operations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:72pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;The Respondent is a wholly owned subsidiary of UGIES and an indirect wholly owned subsidiary of UGI Corporation. The Respondent is authorized to own and operate natural gas transmission facilities and engage in open-access transportation services in Pennsylvania. The Respondent provides transportation services of shipper supplied natural gas through the Sunbury Pipeline. The pipeline consists of approximately 34.4 miles of 20-inch pipeline passing through five central Pennsylvania communities, with associated surface facilities that include measurement and regulation, deliver / receiving equipment, and other ancillary facilities. The pipeline will have a Maximum Allowable Operating Pressure (&#8220;MOAP&#8221;) of 1,480 pounds per square inch and a design capacity of 200,000 Dth / day.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:72pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;The pipeline includes one integrated receiving station containing two receipt point interconnection meters with Transcontinental Gas Pipeline Company (&#8220;Transco&#8221;) and MARC I Pipeline in Lycoming County Pennsylvania. The MARC I Pipeline is part of the interstate Stagecoach Pipeline System (&#8220;Stagecoach&#8221;) operated by Central New York Oil &amp;amp; Gas Company, LLC. There are two separate delivery point interconnection meters to measure delivery of natural gas and two separate receipt point meters to measure receipt of natural gas. The two separate delivery point interconnections are: (1) UGI Central Penn Gas (&#8220;UGI CPG&#8221;) in Northumberland County and (2) with the Hummel gas fired power station in Snyder County.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:72pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;The Respondent has no employees and relies on the operation and administrative services provided by UGIES, as well as by third party contractors for the pipeline&#8217;s operations and maintenance.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-left:36pt;padding-right:18pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:120%;padding-left:11.34pt"&gt;Summary Of Significant Accounting Policies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;a.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:11.34pt"&gt;Basis Of Presentation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:72pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;The accompanying financial statements were prepared in accordance with the accounting and reporting requirements of the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (&#8220;FERC&#8221;) as set forth in its Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases prescribed for Natural Gas Companies, which is a comprehensive basis of accounting other than generally accepted accounting principles (&#8220;GAAP&#8221;). In management&#8217;s opinion, these financial statements reflect all adjustments necessary for a fair presentation of financial position, results of operations, and cash flow for the periods presented.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;b.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:11.34pt"&gt;Use Of Estimates&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:72pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;The preparation of financial statements requires management to make estimates and assumptions that affect the amounts reported in financial statements for assets, liabilities, revenues, expenses, and accompanying notes. These estimates and assumptions are based on management&#8217;s knowledge of current events and / or historical experience that were believed to be reasonable at the time the financial statements were prepared. Actual results could differ from those estimates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;c.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:11.78pt"&gt;Property, Plant, &amp;amp; Equipment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:72pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Property, Plant, &amp;amp; Equipment (&#8220;PP&amp;amp;E&#8221;) is recorded at the original costs of construction. Construction costs include the direct costs of labor, materials and contractor&#8217;s costs, and indirect costs, such as administrative expenses, overheads, and an Allowance For Funds Used During Construction (&#8220;AFUDC&#8221;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;d.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:11.34pt"&gt;Depreciation Expense&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:72pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Annual depreciation expense is based on a projected 40 year life of the Sunbury Pipeline. Using a straight line book depreciation method, the resulting annual depreciation rate for the pipeline assets is 2.5%. The Sunbury project includes installation of ultrasonic metering at its receipt and delivery points. Assuming a 25 year useful life of these ultrasonic meters, the results are an annual depreciation rate of 4%. Based on these assumptions, the FERC, in its Order Issuing Certificate dated April 29, 2016 Docket No. CP15-525-000, approved a composite 2.54% depreciation rate, which is applied to the total depreciable gas plant in service.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;e.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:11.34pt"&gt;Gas Imbalances&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:72pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;In the course of providing natural gas transportation services, the Respondent may receive quantities of natural gas from shippers that differs from the quantities delivered on behalf of shippers, resulting in natural gas transportation imbalances. The Respondent&#8217;s tariff allows shippers to negotiate gas imbalance trading among the parties to reduce the net gas transportation imbalance, in accordance with requirements of the tariff and the Operational Balancing Agreement (&#8220;OBA&#8221;) between the shippers and the Respondent.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:72pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;The Transco and Hummel monthly imbalance is cashed out each month per the OBA. Monthly cash out of Stagecoach and UGI CPG gas imbalances are, at UGIES option only, cashed out if the gas imbalances exceed the Dth threshold balance at the end of the month in the OBA.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;f.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:13.56pt"&gt;Revenue Recognition&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:72pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Revenues are primarily from reservation charges for the transportation of shipper supplied gas pursuant to long term firm Transportation Services Agreements (&#8220;TSA&#8217;s&#8221;). The Respondent&#8217;s revenues are recognized based on the contracted maximum daily quantity of transportation services and billed to the shipper monthly over the contract period regardless of &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:72pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;the volume of natural gas that is transported. The shipper is billed the following month for the total amount of the transportation services rendered for the preceding month.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:72pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;The Respondent&#8217;s tariffs provide for a commodity charge for interruptible transportation services based on the total quantity of natural gas in Dths delivered multiplied by the commodity rate per the TSA. The Respondent would record revenues for interruptible services when physical deliveries of natural gas are made at the agreed upon delivery point.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;g.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:11.34pt"&gt;Pension, Post Retirement Benefits&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:72pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;The Respondent has no employees. Pipeline operations and maintenance services are provided to the Respondent by UGIES. The Respondent reimburses UGIES for the costs of the employees providing these services, which include compensation, employee expenses, and benefit plan costs.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;h.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:11.34pt"&gt;Fuel, Loss, &amp;amp; Unaccounted For Gas Tracker&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:72pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;The Respondent&#8217;s tariff includes a tracking mechanism for Fuel, Loss, &amp;amp; Unaccounted For Gas (&#8220;FL&amp;amp;U&#8221;), which is a regulatory mechanism allowing the Respondent&#8217;s rates to fluctuate in response to changes in line losses and other unaccounted for gas as they occur. The Respondent is required to make annual filings with the FERC, on or before March 1 to become effective April 1, to update the FL&amp;amp;U Adjustment Mechanism (&#8220;FAM&#8221;) to take into account estimated quantities of FL&amp;amp;U natural gas required during the perspective 12 month period and the unrecovered / over recovered FL&amp;amp;U quantities from the preceding 12 month period. The FL&amp;amp;U is subject to regulatory review before it goes into effect. The net under / over recovered FL&amp;amp;U quantities are recorded in Miscellaneous Current &amp;amp; Accrued Assets / Liabilities on the Respondent&#8217;s balance sheet.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;i.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:14.01pt"&gt;AFUDC&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:72pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;AFUDC represents the estimated costs of debt (interest) and equity funds necessary to finance the construction of new regulated facilities. The Respondent included, in its AFUDC calculation, the FERC approved debt / equity split, return on equity, and imputed debt cost. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:72pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;The Respondent financed the pipeline project through contributions from its corporate parent, UGI Energy Services, LLC. For purposes of calculating both AFUDC and the capital structure for its tariff rates, the commission in its Order Issuing Certificate, dated April 29. 2016, CP15-525-000, directed the Respondent to use a capital structure consistent with commission policy, which includes a 50% debt / equity ratio. The Commission also approved the Respondent&#8217;s assumptions on debt costs and return on equity. No AFUDC was calculated during 2024.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;j.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:14.01pt"&gt;Regulatory Assets &amp;amp; Liabilities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:72pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;The Respondent has established a Regulatory Asset to offset the deferred taxes on the equity component of AFUDC accrued on the construction of the pipeline. The taxes on the equity component of AFUDC and the offsetting deferred taxes are included in rate base and cost of service included in the Respondent&#8217;s Application For Certificate Of Public Convenience. In the Commission Order granting the Certificate, the Commission found that the Respondent&#8217;s proposed cost of service and initial recourse rates are consistent with Commission Policy. The unwinding of the regulatory asset commenced effective January 1, 2017, at the time the pipeline was placed into service.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;k.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:11.78pt"&gt;Asset Retirement Obligations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:72pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;The Respondent followed the provisions of ASC 410, Asset Retirement &amp;amp; Environmental Obligations, which would require the Respondent to record the fair value of an asset retirement obligation as a liability in the period in which the Respondent incurs a legal or contractual obligation associated with the retirement of tangible gas plant long lived assets. A segment of the Sunbury Pipeline was placed into service in January 2017, with the remaining portion of the pipeline placed into service on August 1, 2017. There is no regulatory, legal, or contractual obligation at this time to retire any portion of the pipeline assets. Therefore, the fair value of these obligations cannot be determined because the end of the pipeline life is indeterminable.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;l.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:14.01pt"&gt;Related Party Transactions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:72pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;The Respondent&#8217;s related party transactions are with UGIES, UGI CPG, and UGI Central Gas Control. Transactions between the Respondent and related parties are identified in the financial statements as associated company transactions. These charges include construction related services, in addition to operating expenses of administrative and financial operations, transportation fees, cash out, technical support, and overhead costs. These expenses are directly charged or billed using agreed upon cost allocation procedures.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;m.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:9.12pt"&gt;Commitments &amp;amp; Contingencies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:108pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;a.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:11.34pt"&gt;Environmental Matters&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:99pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;The Respondent&#8217;s pipeline operations are subject to extensive and evolving federal, state, and local government laws and regulations intended to protect public health and the environment. To satisfy the requirements of the National Environmental Policy Act, the Respondent prepared an environmental assessment (&#8220;EA&#8221;) for the Sunbury pipeline project. The analysis addressed geology, soils, water resources, wetlands, vegetation, fisheries, wildlife, threatened and endangered species, land use, recreation, and other related items.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:99pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;FERC approved the EA in its Order Issuing Certificate, CP15-525-000, dated April 29, 2016, and stated in its order any state or local permits issued with respect to the jurisdictional facilities must be consistent with the conditions of the certificate. The Respondent is not aware of any material environmental actions with respect to non-compliance with any applicable environmental laws and regulations related to the construction and operation of the Sunbury Pipeline Project.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:108pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;b.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:11.34pt"&gt;Docket CP15-525-000 &#8211; Rate Changes &amp;amp; Three-Year Filing Requirement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:99pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;The Respondent&#8217;s approved Pro Forma Tariff includes, among other things, firm and interruptible transportation services at cost &#8211; based recourse rates, as well as approval to offer service at negotiated rates. Consistent with the FERC precedent, Sunbury is required to file a cost and revenue study at the end of its first three years of jurisdictional service or initiate a general rate case no later than three years to justify its initial approved cost-based firm and interruptible recourse rates. While the final outcome of this matter cannot be predicted with certainty at this time, based upon management&#8217;s evaluation of the Project, estimated cost to complete, and operating experience to date, management does not expect a material adverse effect on the Respondent&#8217;s financial position, operating results, and cash flows as a result of filing the required cost and revenue study. The filing requirement was completed and submitted in the first quarter of 2020&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-left:36pt;padding-right:18pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:120%;padding-left:11.34pt"&gt;Major Customers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Major customers are defined as customers to whom annual sales (gas transportation revenue) represent more than ten percent of Gas Operating Revenues. The loss of a significant portion of operating revenues from these customers could have a material adverse effect on the business. The Respondent has only two customers receiving transportation services on the Sunbury Pipeline: (1) Hummel Gas Gathering Station; and (2) UGI Energy Services, LLC, for delivery of natural gas to the distribution facilities of UGI CPG.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;a.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:11.34pt"&gt;Hummel TSA Requirements&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:72pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;The Hummel Transportation Service Agreement (&#8220;TSA&#8221;) contained certain gas delivery and tariff requirements precedent for both the Respondent and Hummel to include, for example, satisfaction of credit requirements, achievement of closing of Hummel&#8217;s financing, project in-service date, minimum delivery pressure, and gas quality specifications. Certain requirements provide for financial remedies to Hummel for loss, costs or damages, or harm not to exceed a specified amount per day if the Respondent is directly attributable for failure to meet the minimum delivery pressure and gas quality specifications. The Respondent does not believe there will be any non-compliance of these precedent conditions and / or an adverse effect on the Respondent&#8217;s financial position and operations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-left:36pt;padding-right:18pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:120%;padding-left:11.34pt"&gt;Legal Proceedings&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;In the normal course of its business, the Respondent may be named as a defendant in various legal proceedings. The Respondent would accrue a liability related to such matters when an obligation becomes probable and can be estimated. Management is not aware of any legal matters that would have a material impact on the Respondent&#8217;s financial position, results of operations, or cash flows.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:36pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%;padding-left:11.34pt"&gt;Disclosures&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;&#8226;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:15.2pt"&gt;Respondent has no significant financial disclosures to report.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;&#8226;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:15.2pt"&gt;Respondent has no contingent Assets or Liabilities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;&#8226;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:15.2pt"&gt;Respondent has no employees.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;&#8226;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:15.2pt"&gt;See k (above) for asset retirement obligations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;&#8226;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:15.2pt"&gt;Respondent has no environmental credits received during the reporting period.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;&#8226;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:15.2pt"&gt;N/A&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;&#8226;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:15.2pt"&gt;N/A&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;&#8226;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:15.2pt"&gt;Respondent has no retained earnings restrictions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;&#8226;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:15.2pt"&gt;Respondent has no significant financial changes directly affecting gas pipeline operations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;&#8226;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:15.2pt"&gt;Respondent has no unsettled rate proceedings.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;&#8226;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:15.2pt"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;&#8226;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:15.2pt"&gt;Respondent has no significant changes in accounting methods during the year, which had an impact on net income.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;&#8226;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:15.2pt"&gt;N/A&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;&#8226;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:15.2pt"&gt;N/A&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;&#8226;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:15.2pt"&gt;There are no notes reflected specifically for UGI Sunbury, LLC. in the UGI Corporation and Subsidiaries Annual Consolidated Financial Statements&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantDisclosuresRegardingTheFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
  <ferc:CompanyIdentifier id="f-15" contextRef="c-1">C005274</ferc:CompanyIdentifier>
  <ferc:LegalEntityIdentifier id="f-16" contextRef="c-1">C005274</ferc:LegalEntityIdentifier>
  <ferc:FormType id="f-17" contextRef="c-1">2/3-Q</ferc:FormType>
  <ferc:RespondentLegalName id="f-18" contextRef="c-1">UGI Sunbury, LLC</ferc:RespondentLegalName>
  <ferc:ReportYear id="f-19" contextRef="c-1" decimals="0" unitRef="u-1">2026</ferc:ReportYear>
